*takes a deep breath*
WOOHOO!!!!!! I FINALLY ASCENDED!
*takes another deep breath*

This was a lot less eventful than my previous near-ascension (where the
Bell of Opening ran out of charges and I couldn't recharge it), but
exciting nonetheless.

The game started fairly uneventful (no oil lamp) up to the point where
my pet got itself killed. "Oh well", I shrugged, "it just would've
gotten in the way."  Once I found the path to the Mines, I explored my
way to the bottom (using some halfway-decent armor dropped by a dwarf)
and found the luckstone. Minetown altar wasn't co-aligned, so I
continued down further into the Dungeons of Doom. I found Sokoban and
got a Bag of Holding as my prize (much to my delight), only to find that
the minetown tool shop had TWO bags of holding for sale (much to my
annoyance). Somewhere along the way, I decided it was time to identify a
few wands. I engraved with the first wand in my inventory and was told
"You may wish for an object". I did, and got two blessed scrolls of
charging. Another zap told me that the wand was empty (it had spawned as
0:1), so I recharged it and used up another 2 wishes on SDSM (asked for
+2, got +0) and GoP (not sure if I got +0 or +2). Some time later, I
used up the other 2 wishes on a cloan of magic resistance (got +0) and
speed boots. Somewhere around DLVL 15 I found an altar and sacrified
until I got Mjollnir. A barracks further down yielded a silver saber.

When I got to the Quest I was only level 12, so I had to do a bunch of
extra killing by working my way down to Medusa's island, where I met my
first and last master mind flayer (which I dispatched with Mojo and
blessed-genocided soon after) and found that one of the pairs of boots I
had bought granted levitation. Medusa was a pushover (wrapped a towel
around my head and let her look at my shiny armor) and the castle was
cleared in short order, yielding my second Wand of Wishing. I still had
a spare scroll of charging, so I wished for speed boots, a helm of
brilliance, and a T-shirt. Using a few spare scrolls, I enchanted my
weapons up to around +4 and my armors to +2 or +3. At this point, my AC
was around -15. Still not having enough experience, I went back up to
search for more stuff to kill. While running to the up-stairs on one
level, I found a vault teleporter. Inside the vault I found a portal to
Fort Ludios.

Clearing out the fort was rather fun, standing in the doorway and
smiting monsters as they approached me. While clearing out the first
room I noticed that I had leveled up to 14 and that I was eligible for
the quest, but the quest could wait. Croesus's vault gave me enough gold
to max my protection and (AC was around -24 by now) give me several
thousand turns of clairvoyance from a temple priest on a nearby level.

The quest was easy, just as it had been in the past. Lord Surtur was a
total wimp, dying on my first (two-weapon) attack and giving me the Orb
of Fate and the Bell of Opening. A short period of removing unneeded
stuff from my bag of holding and I was on my way back to the castle,
down the trap-doors, and down the staircase into Hell (and I didn't even
fall down the stairs).

Gehennom was actually rather easy with the clairvoyance I had gotten
from a priest using Croesus's gold. Asmodeus and Baelzebub were bribed
with less than 100 zorkmids combined, and I eventually found Vlad's
tower. It was around this point that I level-ported back up to identify
a few rings and then used up one of my remaining wishes on a magic
marker, which I used with a pile of blank scrolls to enchant my weapons
and armor to the max (actually needed 2 markers, since the first one
dried out twice) and blessed-genocide 'L' and 'R' (I had killed a
disenchanter and it weakened my silver saber). Juiblex was only a minor
annoyance (took about 5 tries for my unicorn horn to cure me, then dug
my way out and thwacked him), after which I levitated across his swamp
and proceeded downward. On the way up Vlad's tower, I grabbed an amulet
of life saving on the 2nd floor. Vlad was a pushover (as he usually is)
and kindly gave me his Candelabrum, and then I proceeded downward again.
Orcus provided me with a bit of amusement, followed by a slightly-used
wand of death. At DLVL 46 I found the portal to Rodney's tower, and at
DLVL 49 I found the vibrating square, which I marked with a purple-red
potion.

Using the Orb, I level-ported to Minetown (well, to DLVL3 and then down
a bunch of stairs) to buy 6 candles, which I then affixed to the
Candelabrum. Running back up to the Dungeons of Doom, the Orb of Fate
was kind enough to level-port me again to the wizard tower portal, where
my ascension run began.

I made my way up to Rodney's chamber, opened it up with a wand of
digging, and Rodney himself teleported out to greet me. Shortly
afterward, he met the business end of my wand of death and I grabbed the
spellbook. After working my way out of his tower, I level-ported to the
vibrating square (landed within 15 steps of it) and successfully
performed the invocation. Taking a deep breath, I went down the stairs
into Moloch's sanctum.

The Wizard promptly showed up and stole my Orb of Fate, though a few
zaps from my wand of death (he's quite agile) convinced him to give it
back to me. I slowly worked my way through to Moloch's Temple (secret
door detection is a Good Thing) and began my battle to claim the Amulet.
Moloch's lightning blinded me a few times, but in the end it helped me
by zapping his high priest several times and even finishing him off for
me! I grabbed the Amulet and began to work my way up to the surface.

The journey out of Hell was a bit annoying, as I felt the mysterious
force nearly a dozen times (a few times it only teleported me within the
level), but once I was out of Gehennom it was smooth sailing. Somewhere
along the way, Rodney showed up again (and again received the business
end of my wand of death, after I recharged it). I finally reached level
1, checked my inventory (yep, I've still got the real Amulet), and
climbed up to the Elemental Plane of Earth.

Rodney made his final appearance, again being at the wrong end of my
wand of death (which managed to ricochet and kill the Elvenking for me).
I wrote a scroll of gold detection, chugged down some booze, and found
my way to the Plane of Air (only took 3 zaps from my wand of digging). I
quickly swapped my speed boots for levitation and fought off numerous
air elementals and dragons, dropping almost to half health, though I
managed to catch enough rest inside vortices to fully heal up. I worked
my way to the right side of the level and a monster was nice enough to
stumble into the portal and reveal its location to me. I rushed in...
...and landed (well, floated) in the Plane of Fire.  I slowly worked my
way to the left, killing fire elementals and salamanders and vortices
and demons (oh my!) and then realized that I no longer had a way to
confuse myself. Then I remembered - I'm a valkyrie! I have the Orb of
Fate, and it's still got 5 charges on it. I searched for ^ and made a
run for the portal (with dozens of monsters chasing me), landing finally
on the Plane of Water. I started by killing a few monsters and floating
around, but then I realized I was still levitating and began floating
toward the right side of the level. Upon landing in a large bubble, I
asked the Orb where the portal was and found it was only a few spaces
away. I jumped in and materialized on the Astral Plane.

I landed near the left side, so I figured it'd be best to proceed in
that direction. I met Famine (and smacked him numerous times) as well as
a few priests and dragons (which dropped me below 50% hp, much to my
alarm). I ducked back into the other room and killed the dragons one by
one, using the priest-summoned insects as a shield (allowing me to
regenerate completely). I bashed my way to the left temple and found
that it belonged to Tyr. With a deep breath, I turned around and headed
to the right, killing Famine again on the way. Just before I ran into
Death, I realized I was still levitating, so I switched back to my speed
boots. Death tried his death touch on me a few times, but found that my
weapons were a bit more effective. After he dropped me below 50% HP
again, I killed him and quickly moved onward into the high temple. I ran
onto the altar and looked down. It was Odin's. The rest, as they say, is
history.

On top of all of that, the ascension was made on nethack.alt.org for all
to see. I currently reside in 56th place on the high score list.

